{"id": "EUVD-2026-103919", "enisaUuid": "7f24575f-e1c1-3ef3-ad28-1b97e9866503", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: health: max30102: fix NULL dereference in interrupt handler\n\nThe interrupt is requested in max30102_probe() and stays enabled\nfor the lifetime of the device, but indio_dev->active_scan_mask is only\nvalid while a buffer is enabled. When an interrupt arrives while no\nbuffer is enabled, the handler dereferences the NULL active_scan_mask:\n\n  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0000000000000000\n  Call trace:\n   __bitmap_weight+0x64/0x98 (P)\n   max30102_interrupt_handler+0x48/0x160 [max30102]\n\nCall max30102_fifo_count() at the top of the handler and return early\nunless it reports a FIFO sample is ready. Because FIFO_RDY is the only\ninterrupt source enabled in max30102_chip_init(), an invocation of\nmax30102_interrupt_handler() without the FIFO_RDY interrupt status bit\nset carries no data to read and can return before touching\nactive_scan_mask. A negative return from max30102_fifo_count()\nindicates a failed interrupt status read and is treated the same way.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:44:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:30", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2a74f30a7bb305cdc5c3e3e9239b32bb84f3529f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eeb23ba97bd8016e815ef70300b8d34a0a316b90", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/60699102827fdb51f9591414165359c8e867f302", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8d6f98972fe2bd6f73f39d982af0c85d766a1503", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f0ea4824deebf21dacfbe397c4b0a5fd3e745a8d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-g7xj-pf5g-99j9", "CVE-2026-98665"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1d061dde-b01e-3fc9-8e92-efc7e9f74d37", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.16"}, {"id": "2eb53b78-d2a2-3fdc-bda7-017adfa2f6fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "35a82b42-0b7e-3e8b-83d5-e7fbfbc4135f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "90579b69e94bf11ea0745ff003e82a6ce9725f96 <2a74f30a7bb305cdc5c3e3e9239b32bb84f3529f"}, {"id": "3d29d672-aa53-3457-b86c-b7ea7b9a6cd1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5f5b09bb-e63a-3cee-9b7e-62b99e0127a1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "66ad8bc6-6178-37a9-9e66-4426e3e7a7d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "90579b69e94bf11ea0745ff003e82a6ce9725f96 <8d6f98972fe2bd6f73f39d982af0c85d766a1503"}, {"id": "9a4b835b-43e5-308d-bf59-ac4c2c782612", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "a14e1302-6bac-326d-89a6-93fb60a41772", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "90579b69e94bf11ea0745ff003e82a6ce9725f96 <60699102827fdb51f9591414165359c8e867f302"}, {"id": "cacdaf38-b5d1-3ce7-8385-9d567e88a05e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d578daf2-db06-3f5e-9cc1-73c940b8d6d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "90579b69e94bf11ea0745ff003e82a6ce9725f96 <eeb23ba97bd8016e815ef70300b8d34a0a316b90"}, {"id": "e892c3b2-2e12-3762-89c2-2d81bf96eb35", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "eb4d93d5-6470-3b9e-b60f-23043237a6f7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "90579b69e94bf11ea0745ff003e82a6ce9725f96 <f0ea4824deebf21dacfbe397c4b0a5fd3e745a8d"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b1a7748b-ebd2-352c-b5be-744073efef14", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}